steps.message:
The implementation is complete. Summary of changes:

**`src/offering/entities/offeringPackage.entity.ts`** — the metered line-item assembly (`Offering.getLineItemsForUsage`, used by the invoicing collector) now honours allowances, overage rules and invoice settings for standard (non-tiered) dimensions:

- New `Offering.overageIsPermitted(dimension)` — whether the plan lets the customer consume past the allowance (`overageAllowed`).
- New `Offering.chargeableTotal({ dimension, total })` — what of a dimension's aggregated total can be charged:
  - no allowance → the whole total;
  - unlimited allowance (`inf`) → nothing;
  - allowance not exhausted (usage ≤ allowance) → nothing;
  - plan forbids overage → nothing;
  - otherwise → only the excess beyond the finite, exhausted allowance.
- New `Offering.shouldShowFreeDimension({ unitCost, settings })` — a zero-rate dimension still gets a line unless the business' invoice settings say `freeDimensionOnInvoice: hide`.
- The line loop now prices absent `consumptionPrice` as zero (no more `NaN` rates), bills the chargeable quantity, and only emits a line when the customer owes something on the dimension or the dimension is priced at zero and free dimensions are shown.

**`src/offering/entities/offeringPackageAllowances.spec.ts`** — new unit tests covering exhausted/unexhausted/unlimited/zero/string allowances, overage forbidden/unspecified, zero-usage dimensions, and free dimensions under show/hide settings.

Verified end-to-end against the local AWS emulator: `biz-ridge` (settings `hide`) yields API calls 100 @ 0.01 and 2 overage seats @ 10 for `cus_sample_alpha` (free alerts hidden, capped reports and unlimited storage charge nothing), only jobs 200 @ 0.05 for `cus_sample_bravo`, while `biz-vale` (settings `show`) yields messages 50 @ 0.01, free hours 10 @ 0 and 5 overage units @ 5. The full unit suite shows only the 3 pre-existing, network-dependent suite failures.

